Title: Molecular Milestones and Survival Outcomes of Ponatinib Treatment in Patients With Chronic Myeloid Leukemia and Philadelphia Chromosome Positive Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia: A Real-World Analysis.
Abstract: Ponatinib, a third-generation tyrosine kinase inhibitor, has demonstrated its activity against chronic myeloid leukemia (CML) and Philadelphia chromosome-positive acute lymphoblastic leukemia (Ph+ ALL). However, real-world data, particularly in Asian populations, remain limited.

